Personally, I have always felt that Rodney's harassment of players that reach demigod status should be more interesting.

Right now, every rn1(200, 50) [allmain.c#267] turns
there is a 
1/3 chance of nothing
1/6 chance of curse items
1/6 chance of summon nasties
1/6 chance of aggravate monsters
1/6 chance of Summon Wizard

Thing is, this can get a bit repetitive, and doesn't really feel like the Rodney is throwing everything he's got at you.

I propose a few changes.

1) The intervene() timer should be impacted by luck.
Low luck should both increase the average frequency and increase the unpredictability of the harassment.
This is just an initial proposal but something like rn1((200-Luck), 65-rnl(40))
seems a bit more appropriate. 

2) Expanded list of possible effects:
*nothing
*curse items
*summon nasties
*aggravate monsters
*Summon Wizard
*drop boulders all around the < 
*darken much of the level and remove fuel from light sources the player is carrying
*make the amulets and fake amulets heavier until the next call of intervene() - when this happens, they all have a small chance to fall out of your hands that depends on strength, dexterity, and luck
*sprinkle the level with a few pools (maybe call dogushforth() centered on the player and on one or two random locations
*sprinkle the level with some lava - never under the player (too evil)
*create a hole under the player (or a pit if it is undiggable)
*stinking cloud centered on the player
*maybe others - up to whoever decides to code this


3) Instead of choosing one random effect, there is a chance of several to happen. The selection of abilit(y|ies) should be something like this pseudocode:

First, check to see if Summon Wizard is selected
1/7 chance of Summon Wizard
if you roll Summon Wizard, that is the only effect that happens

Else,
do this LOOP:
{
1/3 chance of EXIT LOOP
else, 
select an ability at random with equal probability
if it is a duplicate effect, EXIT LOOP
if it is the 3rd ability selected and your luck is >=0 or it is the 4th ability selected and your luck is <0, do it, then EXIT LOOP
if it is one you haven't selected, do it, then REPEAT LOOP
}

Note: I know this is a lot of stuff, but I've given this a lot of thought, and I don't think this makes Rodney's harassment significantly more dangerous - it might actually be a bit easier, if less predictable.
It definitely makes the endgame more interesting...


